    {
      "title": "Module 1 \u00b7 Logs of Numbers Less Than 1",
      "html": "<p>If $0<N<1$, then $\\log_{10}N$ is negative. We write it with a <b>bar characteristic</b>: e.g. $\\log 0.023 = \\bar{2}.3617$ meaning $-2 + 0.3617 = -1.6383$.</p><p>Method: shift the decimal so the number is in $[1,10)$; the number of shifts (negated) gives the characteristic.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "State the characteristic of $\\log 0.0025$.",
          "a": "$0.0025 = 2.5\\times 10^{-3}$, so characteristic $=\\bar{3}$ (i.e. $-3$)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 2 \u00b7 Calculations Using Log Tables",
      "html": "<p>Multiply, divide, raise to powers or take roots using $\\log(ab)=\\log a+\\log b$, $\\log(a/b)=\\log a-\\log b$, $\\log a^n = n\\log a$. Read antilog at the end.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p><h4>More key points</h4><ul><li>State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$. \u2014 \\bar{2}.</li><li>State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$. \u2014 \\bar{4}.</li><li>State the characteristic of $\\log 0.04073$. \u2014 \\bar{2}.</li><li>State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00829$. \u2014 \\bar{3}.</li></ul><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Evaluate $\\sqrt{0.4356}$ using logs.",
          "a": "$\\log 0.4356 = \\bar{1}.6390 = -0.3610$. Half: $-0.1805 = \\bar{1}.8195$. Antilog $\\approx 0.6600$."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Module 3 \u00b7 Indices \u2194 Logarithms",
      "html": "<p>The core identity: $b^x = N \\iff \\log_b N = x$. Logarithms are exponents written a different way.</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p><h4>Key points</h4><ul><li>$0.03245 = 3.245\\times 10^{-2}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{2}$.</li><li>$0.00035 = 3.5\\times 10^{-4}$, so characteristic $= \\bar{4}$.</li></ul><h4>Worked example</h4><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.03245$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{2}</p><p><b>Q:</b> State the characteristic of $\\log 0.00035$.<br/><b>A:</b> \\bar{4}</p>",
      "examples": [
        {
          "q": "Rewrite $\\log_5 125 = 3$ in index form.",
          "a": "$5^3 = 125$."
        }
      ]
    },
